<title>UK: BT's network operations inefficient -watchdog.</title>
<headline>BT's network operations inefficient -watchdog.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK telecom watchdog Oftel said on Tuesday British Telecommunications Plc's methods of operation and organisation entailed cost inefficiencies of around 40 million stg per year.</p>
<p>This amount is worth around 3.5 percent of the total costs of BT's network operation, Oftel said in a report.  </p>
<p>&quot;These findings are important to the level at which  'X' is set in the proposed network charge controls on BT,&quot; Oftel said in a statement.</p>
<p>Some of the prices BT charges its customers are capped at a level (X) below retail price inflation by the industry regulator.</p>
<p>But the study that evaluated the efficiency of BT's inland conveyance network concluded that the country's dominant telecoms supplier had a modern digital network and provided a high quality of service overall.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7987</p>
